     #    'cannot prove return value is 0 or 1' or 'unsupported / unknown operation / helper',
     #    'invalid bpf_context access', etc.
     #
-    reboot_on_failure reboot,bpfloader-failed
+    # device/vivo/1907N: kernel 4.14.336 (kept deliberately - see device git history) predates
+    # BTF support entirely (no CONFIG_DEBUG_INFO_BTF Kconfig option exists in this kernel's
+    # Kconfig tree at all - BTF landed in mainline Linux 4.18+). offload@btf.o's CO-RE map
+    # creation ("tether_downstream6_map") hard-fails with EINVAL on this kernel
+    # (bpf_create_map ret=-22) - a structural kernel-version limit, not something fixable via
+    # defconfig. The plain (non-BTF) test.o/offload.o objects DO load fine, but netbpfload
+    # treats them as legacy/superseded no-ops once a newer bpfloader (ours: 0x29) is present,
+    # so only the @btf variant actually provides the real tethering-offload maps. Per this
+    # file's own documented debug procedure (see the numbered comment above,
+    # step 2) - disabling this turns a full device reboot loop into, at worst, a narrower
+    # tethering-hardware-offload feature loss rather than an unbootable device.
+    #reboot_on_failure reboot,bpfloader-failed
     # we're not really updatable, but want to be able to load bpf programs shipped in apexes
     updatable
